  ## Description
  Detect cloud victim data collection behavior.
  
  ## Objective metadata
  
  - **Priority**: High
  - **Type**: Threat
  - **Investment**: Medium
  - **Composition**: Sequence
  - **Composition rationale**: Correlate cloud identity telemetry with control plane actions.
  
  ## Signals
  ### Unusual cloud directory enumeration
  Enumerations from anomalous identities and hosts.
  
  - **Severity**: Moderate incident
  - **Methodology**: Behavioural
  - **Effort**: 3
  #### Data
  
  - **Availability**: Complete
  - **Requirements**: Cloud activity and identity logs
  - **Log sources**: Azure AD AuditLogs, Entra ID SignInLogs
  - **Entities**: Account, Hostname
  #### Detectors
  
  - **Sentinel cloud enumeration baseline** (Microsoft Sentinel): Correlates unusual list operations from cloud identities. ([Reference](https://example.com/detectors/cloud-enumeration))
  #### Examples
  
  1. Baseline KQL sequence for identity enumeration.
     - **Link**: [https://example.com/examples/cloud-enumeration](https://example.com/examples/cloud-enumeration)
  ```sql
  AuditLogs
  | where OperationName has "List"
  | where Result =~ "success"
  | take 1
  
  ```
  
  ## Signal MDR coverage
  | Signal | Downstream MDR rules |
  | --- | --- |
  | Unusual cloud directory enumeration | [Shai-Hulud Sentinel Rule](../Rules/shai-hulud-sentinel-rule.md) (`00000000-0000-4000-8103-000000000001`) |
  
